{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OWNED BY THIS EPIC ON FILE OVERLAP — AND ALREADY FIXED BY IT. Verified, not taken from the ticket text.\n\nSCOPE: WE OWN IT. All three files this ticket declares in its file_impact were last modified by commit\n`199b637b5` — \"0a94: pin a UserIdentityModel contract\" — which is story J4 of THIS epic\n[rebar:0a94-e104-7304-4d85]:\n\n    tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py                        -> 199b637b5\n    tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_conflict_resolution.py    -> 199b637b5\n    tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_quarantine_suppression.py -> 199b637b5\n\nSo the epic's work touched exactly the files this bug concerns. It stays parented here rather than\nmoving to a test-infrastructure epic. (My earlier reading — that this is generic pytest-loader work\nwith no Jira/DC dimension — was right about the SUBJECT but wrong about ownership: ownership follows\nthe edit-set, and the edit-set is ours.)\n\nALREADY FIXED, CONFIRMED TWO WAYS:\n\n1. The helper is now CACHE-FIRST in all three files, not `setdefault`:\n       cached = sys.modules.get(name)      # returns the REGISTERED module\n       ...\n       sys.modules[name] = mod             # not setdefault\n   The defective form (`sys.modules.setdefault(name, mod)` followed by `return mod`, which returns a\n   module that is NOT the registered one) is gone.\n\n2. The ticket's OWN deterministic reproduction passes — the reversed collection order that made the\n   defect fire:\n\n       pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ_conflict_resolution.py \\\n              tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_differ.py -q\n       29 passed\n\n   That ordering is the one that used to lose the `setdefault` race and produce\n   `isinstance(Mutation(...), Mutation) is False`. It is green.\n\nWHY IT WAS LATENT, which the ticket diagnosed correctly: alphabetical collection normally puts\n`test_differ.py` first, so it won the `setdefault` and the suite was green; only a collection-order\nflip (macOS vs Linux) exposed the two live copies of `mutation.py` under one `sys.modules` key.\n\nClosing as `preexisting`: the defect pre-dated this epic (introduced with the test-package\nsubdivision, `5a87f5859`), was latent behind collection order, and was repaired as part of J4's work\non these files rather than by a dedicated change."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785530219417562001,"uuid":"0a412512-5e01-4d0e-b17e-b07f63179634"}